            <ArticleTitle>Is predisposition to NAFLD and obesity communicable?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>419-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2012.03.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A forthcoming article in Nature reveals that inflammasome deficiency disturbs gut microbiota and predisposes to diet-induced obesity and liver disease. The aberrant microbiota and its consequences could be transferred by cohousing mutant and wild-type mice, suggesting that some aspects of metabolic syndrome can be communicable (Henao-Mejia et al., 2012).</AbstractText>
